# Playwright and dev-server safety

Avoid hangs in automated agent runs and long local sessions.

## Never use in agent / CI runs

- `playwright test --debug` — opens inspector, waits forever
- `playwright test --ui` — interactive UI mode (use `pnpm test:ui` only when the user is driving)
- `pnpm test` without chromium scope when validating fixes — use chromium default or `PLAYWRIGHT_ALL_BROWSERS=1` only when explicitly requested

## Preferred commands

```bash
pnpm dev:web                    # rebuild @blocks/ui, then next dev :3004
PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3004 pnpm test
pnpm test:e2e                   # chromium-only via run-playwright.mjs
```

## After editing `packages/ui` or `packages/core`

1. `pnpm build --filter @blocks/ui` (or `pnpm dev:web` for a fresh server)
2. Restart `next dev` — HMR does not pick up dist changes

## If something looks frozen

1. Check for a Playwright inspector window or `--debug` in the terminal command
2. `npx kill-port 3004` then `pnpm dev:web`
3. Full multi-browser suite can take 20m+ — use chromium-only unless cross-browser is required

## Timeouts (enforced by `scripts/run-playwright.mjs`)

- Per-test: 30s (`tests/playwright.config.ts`)
- Whole run wall-clock: 45m default (`PLAYWRIGHT_MAX_MINUTES`)
